claimed: okay-script-secure -- the JSP-level gap left after live/push/resume: declarative page security (web.xml's security-constraint). Front-matter `secure: <scope>` (or `any`) on a page; Site(verify = Some(String => Verified)) checks a bearer token from the Authorization header or, for a browser, the session attribute okay.token (set by api.login(token) from a login page, cleared by api.logout()); Policy.scoped(scope) -> 403 on the wrong scope; no/invalid token -> 302 to the login page (`loginPage:` front-matter or root login.md, with ?next=) when one exists, else the 401 + WWW-Authenticate ladder okay-security's Secure uses; api.Principal.current for a page to read who is in. Enforced per dispatched page (forwards included), and on Site.ws for a secure page's Live socket. okayScript gains okaySecurity.jvm as a main dependency. Tests with SessionIssuer through Site.handle.
